# fn-1-0u5.6 Update Playwright IPC mocks for cache commands

## Description
Update Playwright IPC mocks for cache commands.

## File to modify
- `e2e-playwright/mocks/tauri-ipc.ts`

## Mock handlers to add

```typescript
case 'get_cache_stats':
    return {
        total_tiles: 150,
        total_bytes: 25600000, // ~25MB
        providers: {
            esri: { tiles: 150, bytes: 25600000 }
        }
    };

case 'clear_tile_cache': {
    const provider = args?.provider as string | undefined;
    console.log('[Mock IPC] clear_tile_cache called, provider:', provider);
    // Reset mock cache stats if needed
    return undefined; // void return
}

case 'get_network_status':
    return true; // Online by default, can be overridden per-test
```

## State tracking (optional)
Add mock state to track cache operations for verification in tests:
```typescript
let mockCacheStats = { total_tiles: 150, total_bytes: 25600000, ... };

case 'clear_tile_cache':
    mockCacheStats = { total_tiles: 0, total_bytes: 0, providers: {} };
    return undefined;
```
## Acceptance
- [ ] get_cache_stats mock returns CacheStats structure
- [ ] clear_tile_cache mock handles provider param
- [ ] get_network_status mock returns boolean
- [ ] Mock state resets between tests (or tracks correctly)
- [ ] Playwright tests can run with mocked cache commands
